  "question": {
    "math_academy_id": "q-74170",
    "knowledge_point_id": "cd9167b4-572f-589f-9b94-b62ba57eb28f",
    "knowledge_point": "Finding the Average Value of a Function Given a Graph",
    "problem": "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14013500/assets/f5c51e465dd6c7b5f7a39dee26638d1704a34944b2c14eeaf2cbaf4b2a835ebe.png)\n\nThe graph of the function $f(x),$ which is defined on $[-5,7],$ is shown above. The areas of the regions between the graph and the $x$-axis are $13$, $56$ and $7,$ respectively (from left to right). Find the average value of $f(x)$ on $[-5,7].$",
    "worked_solution": "The average value of a function on a given interval is\n\n$$\n{f}_{\\text{avg}}=\\frac{1}{b-a}{\\int }_{a}^{b}f(x)\\,\\text{d}x.\n$$\n\nHere, we see that\n\n$$\n{\\int }_{-5}^{7}f(x)\\,\\text{d}x=-13+56-7=36.\n$$\n\nSo, applying the average value formula, we find that the average value is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}_{\\text{avg}} & =\\frac{1}{b-a}{\\int }_{a}^{b}f(x)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{7-(-5)}\\cdot (36) \\\\  & =\\frac{36}{12} \\\\  & =3.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
