    "reasoning": "All 16 selected answers agree with their own captured worked solutions and are mathematically correct. Two solutions contain authored errors despite giving correct requested answers: q-140583 correctly gives a=2, but its final area expression incorrectly adds the negative integral on [2,5/2]; that integral must be subtracted. q-117444 incorrectly uses lower limit -3 in the displayed integral for the second region and calls the integral on [-3,6] negative, although it equals zero. The second region requires -∫_3^6(9-x²)dx; the subsequent calculation and total 72 are correct. Independently: q-14267 integrates to e^{-y}=C-e^x, and the initial condition gives C=3, hence y=-ln(3-e^x), valid for x<ln 3. q-103912 and q-78234 follow by dividing by 18. q-2472 has average value 4, so 2c=4 gives c=2. q-30776 has integral -8 and interval length 2, giving -4. q-74170 has signed integral -13+56-7=36 and interval length 12, giving 3. q-73894 changes sign at -3. q-140583 changes sign at 2 within the specified interval. q-54475 has two areas of 1/8, totaling 1/4. q-140607 has areas 10/3 and 11/6, totaling 31/6. q-117444 has two areas of 36, totaling 72. q-54522 is positive on (-1,0) and negative on (0,1), requiring the selected signed split. q-116107 completes the squares to (x+3)²-8(y-3)²=8, giving center (-3,3). q-49934 uses -3x²-18x+6=3[11-(x+3)²] and the inverse-sine integral. For q-73487, only interval III is closed and avoids the undefined point x=0. For q-129221, only interval II is closed and lies where sin x>0. No submitted grades were supplied; the MA evidence below comes exclusively from each question's captured worked solution.",
